{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"581f45644d92803ae8652802eb862b4a313c03ba3a4d2e7508d07c24e6dd4b6b","digest":{"component_or_area":"code-reading gates (review-plan and related)","key_entities":["rebar.llm.gate_source.resolve_gate_handle","rebar.signing._gate_commit_sha","rebar._build_info.COMMIT","hatch_build.py","verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets","rebar.toml"],"problem_keywords":["gate run","build drift","stale code","base ref","code-reading gate","warning","commit ancestry"],"propositions":["A gate run does not warn when its running build commit is behind the base ref it pins, allowing old code to review new material silently.","When a gate reads an unknown config key from a newer base ref snapshot, it emits 'typo?' wording that misdirects the operator, rather than indicating the build may predate the key.","The gate must detect when the running build's commit is a strict ancestor of the pinned sha and emit a single advisory warning per (build sha, pinned sha) pair, without failing the run or altering its verdict.","When build provenance is unavailable or the build sha is not present in the target repo (different repositories), the gate must remain silent and not emit a warning."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787519933133886001,"uuid":"f2a432bc-95f3-4bb2-baa9-c769ed0e9210"}